00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.815
they're taking extra precaution and steps

00:03:01.815 --> 00:03:04.930
to make sure that the
virus is not finding itself

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:06.530
here in the US.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:08.125
Again, the huge majority of these cases,

00:03:08.125 --> 00:03:10.680
the 20,000 cases are in China.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.470
There's only 11 cases in the US

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:15.231
and we wanna keep that
number as low as possible.

00:03:15.231 --> 00:03:16.753
What is the CDC doing?

00:03:16.753 --> 00:03:18.380
Well, first and foremost,

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.020
we've increased screening to 20 airports,

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:22.480
we've also decreased the amount of flights

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.400
coming from China to the US.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.630
And now if you're a foreign national,

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:28.290
meaning that you're not a US citizen,

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.830
and you're not a direct
relative of a US citizen,

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:32.810
if you're from China, or you've recently

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:34.447
visited China within the last 14 days.

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:37.930
You will not be allowed to
visit the US during this time.

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:39.514
On top of it, if you are a citizen

00:03:39.514 --> 00:03:42.210
and you're coming back
from the area in China,

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:43.616
known as the Hubei province,

00:03:43.616 --> 00:03:45.441
apologize if I'm mispronouncing that,

00:03:45.441 --> 00:03:48.330
that's the area where the
virus first broke out.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:49.523
Wuhan is the main city there,

00:03:49.523 --> 00:03:51.854
you're gonna be held in
quarantine for 14 days.

00:03:51.854 --> 00:03:53.678
So if you're coming from that city,

00:03:53.678 --> 00:03:56.240
you're coming back to
the US and your citizen

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:58.140
or you're a family
member of a citizen here.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.300
14 days quarantine just to me make sure

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.210
you don't have the virus
'cause the worst thing

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:04.090
that can happen is, if
you come from that area,

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:05.998
you don't know if you have the virus yet.

00:04:05.998 --> 00:04:08.410
You go into the public,
you get a little sick,

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:09.527
you think it's a regular cold,

00:04:09.527 --> 00:04:11.481
but it's really this novel, Corona virus.

00:04:11.481 --> 00:04:14.574
You can get a lot of
people sick very quickly.

00:04:14.574 --> 00:04:17.622
It is quite infectious,
much like the regular flu.

00:04:17.622 --> 00:04:19.590
I'm gonna be talking about that in a bit.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:22.260
As an interesting fact, the
last time we had this type

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:24.677
of quarantine period
happened in the 1960s,

00:04:24.677 --> 00:04:26.148
with the smallpox epidemic.

00:04:26.148 --> 00:04:27.920
For those of you who don't know,

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:31.289
we've eradicated smallpox,
thanks to vaccinations.

00:04:31.289 --> 00:04:34.114
Which is why I'm very pro vaccinations,

00:04:34.114 --> 00:04:35.770
obviously, not for just that reason.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.560
But it's an important thing to know.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:39.400
Something else the CDC is doing is

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.015
it's working in partnership with the FDA

00:04:41.015 --> 00:04:42.636
to accelerate the approval process

00:04:42.636 --> 00:04:45.806
for the testing that's
happening for the corona virus.

00:04:45.806 --> 00:04:48.765
Which at this time can only
be done at CDC headquarters

00:04:48.765 --> 00:04:51.930
in Atlanta, the whole
process really takes anywhere

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:54.633
from 24 to 36 hours, which
is quite a long time.

00:04:54.633 --> 00:04:56.800
Hopefully, they're able to accelerate

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.680
this approval process
and get that process down

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.310
to somewhere like four to
six hours and get the test

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:04.500
spread outside of just the CDC lab.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.800
That's the goal, it's
a lot easier to test it

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:08.805
in a Regional Hospital
sites than having to ship

00:05:08.805 --> 00:05:10.602
the test to CDC every single time.

00:05:10.602 --> 00:05:13.130
You may have seen some
headlines that call this

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:15.049
Corona virus outbreak and epidemic.

00:05:15.049 --> 00:05:16.435
Those headlines are correct.

00:05:16.435 --> 00:05:19.120
Some have said that it's
gonna be a pandemic.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:20.880
You might be wondering,
what's the difference.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:24.243
Well, an epidemic is a
spiking cases in a given area.

00:05:24.243 --> 00:05:27.571
A pandemic is a worldwide
spread affecting many countries

00:05:27.571 --> 00:05:30.120
with large numbers of people infected.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.413
It has not yet been
ruled to be a pandemic,

00:05:32.413 --> 00:05:34.457
by the World Health Organization,

00:05:34.457 --> 00:05:36.494
or pretty much any health organization.

00:05:36.494 --> 00:05:38.710
That being said, it's very possible that

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:40.120
it may turn into a pandemic.

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:41.814
But again, these are just definitions.

00:05:41.814 --> 00:05:45.490
They don't really mean
anything for you and I

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:46.790
on day to day terms.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:49.780
In fact, what I take
away from the possibility

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:51.391
of this becoming a pandemic,
and I certainly hope

00:05:51.391 --> 00:05:53.239
that it doesn't continue to spread,

00:05:53.239 --> 00:05:56.240
is that the countries that
are going to be affected

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:57.903
most by this disproportionately?

00:05:57.903 --> 00:06:01.407
Are those that are the low
socio economic countries.

00:06:01.407 --> 00:06:04.507
Ones that don't have a
modern healthcare system.

00:06:04.507 --> 00:06:06.568
You think about certain
countries in Africa,

00:06:06.568 --> 00:06:09.017
India, where there's
high rates of poverty.

00:06:09.017 --> 00:06:11.580
You're gonna have individuals,
they're gonna be dying

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:13.814
from this simply because
they don't have access

00:06:13.814 --> 00:06:15.400
to supportive care.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:17.270
You may remember that
in the previous video

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:19.846
that I did on this virus, I
said that there is no treatment.

00:06:19.846 --> 00:06:22.078
While there's no treatment,
we can definitely

00:06:22.078 --> 00:06:23.750
give supportive care.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:26.477
Just recently, the NIH
Director came out and said,

00:06:26.477 --> 00:06:30.481
about 20% of these cases require
intensive care monitoring.

00:06:30.481 --> 00:06:33.349
This is usually in the form
of mechanical ventilation.

00:06:33.349 --> 00:06:35.747
And if you live in an area
where that's not available,

00:06:35.747 --> 00:06:37.670
it's very possible that one in five people

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:39.900
will continue losing
their lives and certainly

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:41.899
low GDP countries will
not be able to build

00:06:41.899 --> 00:06:45.820
1000 bed hospital in the
center of a city in 10 days

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:47.619
like they just did in China.

00:06:47.619 --> 00:06:50.489
In fact, I believe that
center did just open today,

00:06:50.489 --> 00:06:52.747
and its sole purpose is to help those

00:06:52.747 --> 00:06:55.000
who are suffering with the Coronavirus.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.010
Now let's move on to
things that we've learned

00:06:57.010 --> 00:06:59.216
about this virus that we didn't
know from the first video.

00:06:59.216 --> 00:07:01.151
Again, this is a lower respiratory tract

00:07:01.151 --> 00:07:04.119
type of virus that your body
really needs to fend off

00:07:04.119 --> 00:07:05.320
on its own.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:07.350
The primary symptoms are fever, cough

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:08.610
and shortness of breath.

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:10.920
If you're experiencing
those and you've recently

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:12.890
visited China or you have some relatives

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:14.590
or friends that have visited China.

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:16.700
You should right away,
call your health provider,

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:18.730
let them know that you're
coming with these symptoms.

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:20.158
So they can prepare the waiting area

00:07:20.158 --> 00:07:22.453
so as to not get any extra people sick,

00:07:22.453 --> 00:07:24.732
especially those with
compromised immune systems.

00:07:24.732 --> 00:07:26.310
New things that we've learned.

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:28.650
First, you may remember
that I mentioned something

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:31.130
about a symptomatic spread of this virus.

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.006
And it was something that
we were really concerned.

00:07:33.006 --> 00:07:34.602
Let me explain that a bit further.

00:07:34.602 --> 00:07:37.140
Those who are infected with the virus

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:38.560
but are not showing symptoms,

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:39.790
meaning that they don't have a fever,

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:41.070
cough or shortness of breath,

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.090
they can technically spread the virus.

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:44.490
We found out this to be true.

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:46.907
Now the cases where they
have spread the virus,

00:07:46.907 --> 00:07:48.736
these asymptomatic individuals,

00:07:48.736 --> 00:07:50.522
the cases have been rather mild.

00:07:50.522 --> 00:07:53.438
Also, when we look back at
the history of past pandemics,

00:07:53.438 --> 00:07:55.079
the main drivers of these viruses

00:07:55.079 --> 00:07:57.705
have been those who have been ill.

00:07:57.705 --> 00:07:59.704
In fact this virus is quite similar

00:07:59.704 --> 00:08:01.710
in the way that it spreads
and the way that it gets

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:04.233
people sick to our
current Influenza virus.

00:08:04.233 --> 00:08:05.847
And I bring that up specifically

00:08:05.847 --> 00:08:07.625
to put things into perspective.

00:08:07.625 --> 00:08:10.530
There's so many people that are worried

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:12.690
about the coronavirus
here in the United States.

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:15.003
There's 11 people with
zero people have died.

00:08:15.003 --> 00:08:18.944
Just this flu season, there
have been more than 19 million

00:08:18.944 --> 00:08:20.898
cases of the Influenza virus.

00:08:20.898 --> 00:08:23.713
There have been over
180,000 hospitalizations

00:08:23.713 --> 00:08:27.535
and over 10,000 deaths the Influenza virus

00:08:27.535 --> 00:08:30.140
is what is a serious threat to our health.

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:32.550
And I see many patients
that have not yet gotten

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:35.256
their flu shot, get your flu
shot 'cause the Influenza virus

00:08:35.256 --> 00:08:38.347
is a real threat and it's
imminent and it's here now.

00:08:38.347 --> 00:08:41.190
We're gonna talk about how
coronavirus is gonna evolve

00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:43.540
and what can happen
next steps but right now

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.980
you can protect yourself against Influenza

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:47.200
by getting vaccinated.

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:49.970
I'll be saying the same thing
if we do create a vaccine

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:51.756
in time for the corona virus as well.

00:08:51.756 --> 00:08:54.330
And if you're interested
in ways you can stay safe

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:55.709
whether you're traveling or not.

00:08:55.709 --> 00:08:57.670
I gave all those tips in my first video

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:59.170
definitely check that out.

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:01.160
Another interesting thing we've learned is

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:03.530
that this virus can spread
through the digestive tract,

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:05.180
meaning the fecal oral route.

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:07.025
So countries that have poor sanitation,

00:09:07.025 --> 00:09:09.413
they could be facing
even a bigger challenge.

00:09:09.413 --> 00:09:13.433
And currently, there is no
evidence that the Corona virus

00:09:13.433 --> 00:09:17.640
this specific novel, Corona
virus can affect your pets.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:20.887
And I say that because
there's been a ton of people

00:09:20.887 --> 00:09:23.820
ordering these face
masks for their poor pets

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:26.330
thinking that they're
gonna protect them somehow

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:27.163
with these masks.

00:09:27.163 --> 00:09:29.584
No, you're not and the WHO has been clear,

00:09:29.584 --> 00:09:32.171
there's been no threat
to your pets at home.

00:09:32.171 --> 00:09:33.960
Bear doesn't need a mask.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:35.143
Speaking of face masks,

00:09:35.143 --> 00:09:37.621
this has been a major
unintended consequence

00:09:37.621 --> 00:09:41.780
of all of this news coverage
and hype and misinformation

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:44.847
about this virus that
people have bought so many

00:09:44.847 --> 00:09:47.822
of these face mask that
they're running out of supply

00:09:47.822 --> 00:09:50.020
for hospital systems.

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:52.460
Look, the reason we need
these surgical masks

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:54.810
the inexpensive ones
that go around the mouth

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:57.892
and wrap around the ears is
because if someone is sick

00:09:57.892 --> 00:10:00.816
with the corona virus and
Influenza, Common cold

00:10:00.816 --> 00:10:03.250
is good for patients to wear them

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:04.780
so that they don't get us sick.

00:10:04.780 --> 00:10:07.530
It's meant for those who
are sick to not transmit,

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:09.210
not for you to stay safe.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:11.639
There's no recommendation
from any organization

00:10:11.639 --> 00:10:13.952
that you at home need one of these masks,

00:10:13.952 --> 00:10:15.630
leave it to the professionals.

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:18.284
And I've seen some absolutely
crazy Instagram posts

00:10:18.284 --> 00:10:21.496
of certain influencers posing
with some of these masks

00:10:21.496 --> 00:10:23.214
showing how stylish they are.

00:10:23.214 --> 00:10:24.972
This is medical equipment,

00:10:24.972 --> 00:10:27.572
the fact that we're having
shortages of it puts medical

00:10:27.572 --> 00:10:30.701
professionals at risk, and
that's absolutely crazy to me.

00:10:30.701 --> 00:10:33.790
I wanna share a quick story of
something my patient told me

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:36.110
just a couple of days ago
that has me concerned.

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:38.610
So my patient who happens
to be Asian descent

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:41.095
told me that a couple of days
ago because they take the bus

00:10:41.095 --> 00:10:43.047
every day from New Jersey
to New York for work.

00:10:43.047 --> 00:10:45.385
People stopped sitting next to them

00:10:45.385 --> 00:10:47.730
because they're worried
about this Coronavirus

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:49.250
'cause it comes from China.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.000
And that's just really disappointing.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:53.530
That type of xenophobia
doesn't belong here in the US.

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:54.550
We're better than that.

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:56.540
There's only 11 cases here in the US,

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:58.800
none in the New York, New Jersey area

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:01.162
and forgetting that we
should not be Xenophobic.

00:11:01.162 --> 00:11:04.600
We should not be racist, we
should not be labeling anyone

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:07.119
that's never ideal look, you
know, I don't stand for that.

00:11:07.119 --> 00:11:08.899
And I hope that we can all do better.

00:11:08.899 --> 00:11:12.175
Finally, I wanna give a huge
shout out to all the doctors,

00:11:12.175 --> 00:11:14.345
health professionals, first responders

00:11:14.345 --> 00:11:16.331
that are working on combating this

00:11:16.331 --> 00:11:18.083
novel Corona virus out there.

00:11:18.083 --> 00:11:20.042
There's actually groups of researchers

00:11:20.042 --> 00:11:24.386
traveling from the WHO to
Wuhan, China to help fight this

00:11:24.386 --> 00:11:26.040
to learn more about it.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:27.900
And we have to give them a huge thank you.

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:30.396
In fact, just the other day
we lost the first doctor

00:11:30.396 --> 00:11:33.451
to this novel Coronavirus in Wuhan, China

00:11:33.451 --> 00:11:35.160
and that's always unfortunate.

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:37.619
We as health care providers
put our lives on the line

00:11:37.619 --> 00:11:39.871
every time something like this happens.

00:11:39.871 --> 00:11:41.550
I think that's really important to say.

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:44.550
Finally, stay alert, not anxious.

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:47.870
Don't allow these media entities
that put scary headlines

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:49.840
out there to make you panic.

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:51.148
If you want quality information,

00:11:51.148 --> 00:11:56.148
visit the CDC, WHO, NIH websites
or tune in and check out

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:59.280
my videos I'm gonna be delivering messages

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:01.290
from those sources and giving you the most

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:02.590
up to date information.

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:06.120
Remember this video
filmed February 3rd 2020.

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:08.400
If you wanna see my first
video on the Coronavirus,

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:11.123
click here and as always
stay happy and healthy.

